          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Unnamed first-person narrator\",\"addressee\":\"Maria\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig. Jeg elsker Dig i Lyst og i\\nNød, Hverdage og Festdage. Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil\\njeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig. Javel har jeg længtes efter\\nmin yndige Elskerindes Kærtegn. Men mest har jeg længtes efter alt\\ndet andet, som ogsaa er Dig: dit trofaste Hjærte, din rene Tanke,\\ndin milde Tale, dit lyse Smil, som er min Sol i Tvivlen, dit gode\\nHaandtryk, som er min Styrke paa Vejen.\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The focal expression directly avows the narrator's present love for Maria. Its truth-presenting force is reinforced by the oath-like assurance that he habitually understates rather than exaggerates his feelings and by his immediate repetition of the avowal.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig. Jeg elsker Dig i Lyst og i\\nNød, Hverdage og Festdage.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.91,\"reason\":\"In this occurrence, “I love you” answers Maria's concern that his feeling may be temporary and is immediately expanded into constancy through hardship and ordinary life, followed by a declared intention to share a long life with her. Thus the focal avowal also affirms an enduring relational commitment. It is not a formally specified promise, but the shared-life language is part of the same answer and establishes undertaking force rather than merely supplying a separate nearby promise.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker Dig i Lyst og i\\nNød, Hverdage og Festdage. Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil\\njeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"For det er jo sandt, ikke noget, Du imorgen fortryder, ikke\\nnoget, Du nu bilder Dig ind, fordi Du har længtes en Smule efter din\\nElskerinde?\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.92,\"reason\":\"Although the reunion is highly emotional, the focal expression is a deliberate, reasoned reply to Maria's question, supported by an assurance and detailed explanation. The supplied evidence does not present it as a reflex-like cry or expressive discharge beyond its avowing and committing functions.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg svarer: »Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"reason\":\"The expression also reassures Maria and answers her request for confirmation, but those functions are adequately accounted for by its truth-presenting avowal and contextually affirmed commitment. No distinct residual core mode is established.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"For det er jo sandt, ikke noget, Du imorgen fortryder, ikke\\nnoget, Du nu bilder Dig ind, fordi Du har længtes en Smule efter din\\nElskerinde?«\\n\\nJeg svarer:\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"At their reunion, Maria asks whether the narrator's apparent change is real, durable, and not something he will regret the next day or mistake for merely missing his lover. He answers her directly with the focal avowal and elaborates it as love extending across pleasure, hardship, ordinary days, celebrations, and a long shared life.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The same turn affirms that the narrator is committed to loving Maria across changing circumstances and intends to live with her for a long time. The precise institutional or practical terms of that shared life are not stated. Maria's tears of happiness and her understanding that he speaks truly represent positive uptake of his reassurance and relational commitment.\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not recognise the specific work from the supplied passages.\",\"limitations\":\"The evidence strongly establishes the represented avowal, affection, and Maria's immediate uptake, but it does not specify a formal promise, marriage arrangement, or detailed terms of the proposed shared life. It also cannot independently verify the narrator's future fulfilment of the commitment.\"}"
        }
